# Working artifacts produced while analysing tradingpro-main.zip.
#
# CHANGED: the unpacked app tree is now TRACKED, because it has to be deployable.
# Vercel deploys from a Git repository, and while `extracted/` was ignored the app
# existed only as a patch file plus a build script — and gitignored content is not
# persisted between turns, so the tree kept vanishing. `analysis/restore-workspace.sh`
# still rebuilds it from tradingpro-main.zip + analysis/patches/applied-so-far.patch,
# which remains the record of exactly what the audit changed and why.
#
# Still ignored: dependencies, generated databases, and anything else under extracted/.
extracted/*
!extracted/tradejournal/
node_modules/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Downloaded historical OHLCV used by analysis/candle-shim.js.
# These are third-party datasets fetched via api.github.com, not project
# source, so they are reproducible rather than tracked. See the provenance
# table in the header of analysis/candle-shim.js.
analysis/fixtures/
analysis/*.log

# Verbatim course transcripts pulled from github.com/nedu-m/market-mechanics-bot
# and used only to audit the strategy implementation. Third-party copyrighted
# material — the findings are recorded in ANALYSIS.md section 10.2, so the raw
# text is reproducible rather than tracked.
analysis/transcripts/

# The same repo's STRATEGY_SPEC.md and RESULTS.md, fetched for the independent
# cross-check in ANALYSIS.md section 11. That repo declares no license, so the
# files stay untracked; every figure relied on is quoted in the report, with the
# source repo named so it can be re-fetched.
analysis/independent/
